M2b checkpoint update (2026-11-15)
-----------------------------------

XIRI_IP30_M2B continues past M2a into main() and autoconfiguration.

* heart0 attaches at mainbus addr 0x0ff00000.  Its driver owns the 64-bit
  HEART ISR/IMR set, maps ISR bits 0-15/16-31/32-49/50/51-63 to CPU
  IP2..IP6, installs platform.intr_establish and masks/clears all vectors.
* XIRI_IP30 uses a dedicated IPL map that masks IP2..IP6 at IPL_VM and
  above; heart_intr_establish accepts vectors 0..63 at IPL_VM only.
  heart_bus_reset() is a no-op so autoconfiguration cannot erase attached
  device masks.  Event-counter names are persistent per handler.
* The attach self-test verifies set, masked-pending, unmask and clear
  semantics and prints XIRI_IP30_M2B_HEART_OK.
* consinit() keeps the ARCS64 console on IP30 until IOC3 is implemented.
* mips3_initclocks() supplies CP0 Count/Compare hardclock and the
  mips3 timecounter.  A five-tick callout prints
  XIRI_IP30_M2B_CLOCK_OK heart_delta=0xb3cee clockints=5 ticks=5, gated on
  the HEART self-test.  It then installs a HEART vector-0 handler at
  IPL_VM, verifies splvm() defers the pending ISR bit, and observes
  delivery after splx: XIRI_IP30_M2B_INTR_OK masked=deferred delivered=1.
  Explicit HEART/CLOCK/INTR failure markers fail the probe.
* The boot reaches `boot device: <unknown>` / `root device:` with no root
  storage configured.  That is a checkpoint, not a full boot.
* M1, O2 single-user and Indy64 single-user regressions still pass.

Still unproven: cache-error delivery, physical hardware, IOC3 serial,
XIO/Bridge/PCI, storage, root mount, networking and multi-user login.
Next: native IOC3 serial and the M3 bus/PCI path; cache-error injection
remains explicitly deferred.


